{"name":"Golden Marguerite","hex":"#fdcc37","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of, or relating to, gold.","Having a color or other richness suggestive of gold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Can we verify this sense?) brassy drummer, brassy chub, etc. (Kyphosus vaigiensis), a fish found in southeast Asia.","Ellipsis of golden retriever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden"},{"term":"marguerite","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An oxeye daisy (Leucanthemum vulgare).","A shrub with daisy-like flowers, Argyranthemum frutescens"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marguerite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cota tinctoria","blocks":[{"text":"Cota tinctoria, the golden marguerite, yellow chamomile, or oxeye chamomile, is a species of perennial flowering plant in the sunflower family. Other common names include dyer's chamomile, Boston daisy, and Paris daisy. In horticulture this plant is still widely referred to by its synonym Anthemis tinctoria."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Anthemis_April_2009-1.jpg/330px-Anthemis_April_2009-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cota_tinctoria","wikidata":"Q15551906"},{"title":"Marguerite (2015 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Marguerite is a 2015 French-language comedy-drama film directed by Xavier Giannoli and written by Giannoli and Marcia Romano, loosely inspired by the life of Florence Foster Jenkins. The film is an international co-production among France, the Czech Republic, and Belgium. Marguerite received eleven nominations at the 41st César Awards, winning for Best Actress, Best Costume Design, Best Sound, and Best Production Design."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1c/Marguerite_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marguerite_(2015_film)","wikidata":"Q20647699"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Bloem_van_Anthemis_lemon._18-06-2024._%28d.j.b%29.jpg/500px-Bloem_van_Anthemis_lemon._18-06-2024._%28d.j.b%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Bloem_van_Anthemis_lemon._18-06-2024._%28d.j.b%29.jpg/1280px-Bloem_van_Anthemis_lemon._18-06-2024._%28d.j.b%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Bloem_van_Anthemis_lemon._18-06-2024._%28d.j.b%29.jpg/500px-Bloem_van_Anthemis_lemon._18-06-2024._%28d.j.b%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Inflorescence.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABloem_van_Anthemis_lemon._18-06-2024._(d.j.b).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Bloem_van_een_gele_kamille_%28Cota_tinctoria%29_24-06-2026._%28actm.%29.jpg/500px-Bloem_van_een_gele_kamille_%28Cota_tinctoria%29_24-06-2026._%28actm.%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Bloem_van_een_gele_kamille_%28Cota_tinctoria%29_24-06-2026._%28actm.%29.jpg/1280px-Bloem_van_een_gele_kamille_%28Cota_tinctoria%29_24-06-2026._%28actm.%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Blo